  "So far our functions **printed** results. Often you want a function to **give back** a value so you can use it later. That is what **`return`** does.\n\n`def add(a, b):`\n`    return a + b`\n\n`total = add(3, 4)` → `total` is 7.\n\nKey ideas:\n\n- `return` sends a value back to the caller and **ends the function immediately**.\n- A function without `return` gives back `None`.\n- **print vs return:** print only shows a value on screen; return hands it back so the program can keep working with it.\n- You can return several values as a tuple: `return low, high`.",
  "Hozirgacha funksiyalarimiz natijani **chiqarardi**. Koʻpincha funksiya qiymatni **qaytarib berishi** kerak, toki uni keyin ishlata olaylik. Buni **`return`** qiladi.\n\n`def add(a, b):`\n`    return a + b`\n\n`total = add(3, 4)` → `total` 7 ga teng.\n\nAsosiy gʻoyalar:\n\n- `return` qiymatni chaqiruvchiga qaytaradi va **funksiyani darhol tugatadi**.\n- `return` siz funksiya `None` qaytaradi.\n- **print va return:** print qiymatni faqat ekranda koʻrsatadi; return esa uni qaytarib beradi, dastur u bilan ishlashda davom eta oladi.\n- Bir nechta qiymatni kortej sifatida qaytarish mumkin: `return low, high`.",
